<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n14172" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπουρ-ίζω</span></b> , (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὖρος</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὅρος</span>
			) only in <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				22.489
			</span></i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄλλοι γάρ οἱ ἀπουρίσσουσιν</span>
			(lon. for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀφοριοῦνται,</span> Sch.Ven.A)
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀρούρας</span> others <i>will mark
				off the boundaries of</i> his fields, i.e. <i>take</i> them
				<i>away from</i> him; better <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπουρήσουσι</span>
			<i>will take away;</i> cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπούρας.</span>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				v.l. for
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπουρίζω</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				1.668
			</span></i>.</div>
